IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wca-core`
IMPORT `wca-seat`
IMPORT `wca-seat-insurer`

-- Cases for the insurer's seat (wca-seat-insurer.l4), the insurer's regulative rules in wca-core.l4, and MIRROR CASES:
-- the same facts asked from the worker's seat (wca-seat.l4), with answers that agree. Every expected value was worked
-- by hand from the deposited text (A1951-2.txt), never copied from the encoding's output. HYPOTHETICAL throughout.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not.

`2 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 11 2026
`5 Nov 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 11 2026
`20 Nov 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2026
`30 Nov 2026` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 11 2026
`1 Dec 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2026
`4 Dec 2026`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 4 12 2026
`26 Jan 2027` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 26 1 2027
`3 Nov 2027`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 11 2027

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE I1. The medical certificate (s 116(2), s 118(2), s 119). A claim for weekly compensation received 5 November.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Is the claim taken to comply with the certificate requirement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim complies with s 118(2)`
-- Deficient, flagged in writing within 72 hours: the claim is not made until a complying certificate comes.
#ASSERT `Is the claim taken to comply with the certificate requirement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is not made until a complying medical certificate is given (s 119(2))`
-- MIRROR (worker's seat): the worker's claim is made on 20 November, when the complying certificate is given.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim made` `5 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `20 Nov 2026`
-- Deficient, not flagged within 72 hours: taken to comply.
#ASSERT `Is the claim taken to comply with the certificate requirement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim is taken to comply with s 118(2) (s 119(3))`
-- MIRROR (worker's seat): made on 5 November.
#ASSERT `On what day is my claim made` `5 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `5 Nov 2026`
-- Deficient and flagged, but waived (s 119(4)).
#ASSERT `Is the claim taken to comply with the certificate requirement` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the insurer waived compliance with s 118(2) (s 119(4))`
-- A lump sum claim: no s 116(2) certificate is needed.
#ASSERT `Is the claim taken to comply with the certificate requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claim complies with s 118(2)`
-- 72 hours.
#ASSERT `Within how many hours must I flag a deficient certificate` TRUE EQUALS 72

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE I2. Acceptance by silence (s 128). Claim received 2 November 2026; the 28 days end on 30 November.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted the claim` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the claim is taken to be accepted at the end of` `30 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted the claim` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `30 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the claim is not taken to be accepted: the insurer decided to reject it within 28 days`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted the claim` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `1 Dec 2026` EQUALS `the claim is taken to be accepted at the end of` `30 Nov 2026`
-- MIRROR (worker's seat): the same facts give the same answer.
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted the claim` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `Is my claim taken to be accepted` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have accepted the claim` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `30 Nov 2026` EQUALS `Is my claim taken to be accepted` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `30 Nov 2026`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE I3. Stopping weekly compensation after a rejection (ss 129-132, s 134). Claim given 2 November 2026.
-- Answers: claim given; rejection received; reasons given; only ground no time; leave; order states a day; the day
-- stated; the day the worker got notice.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Rejected 20 November (day 18): from 4 December 2026 (s 130(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` `4 Dec 2026` "s 130(1)(a)"
-- MIRROR (worker's seat).
#ASSERT `From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`
-- Rejected 1 December (day 29): from 26 January 2027 (s 131(a)), and the worker's seat agrees.
#ASSERT `From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `weekly compensation may stop from` `26 Jan 2027` "s 131(a)"
#ASSERT `From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `From what day may my weekly compensation stop after a rejection` `2 Nov 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`
-- Rejected 3 November 2027 without leave: no effect (s 132(1)).
#ASSERT `From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `3 Nov 2027` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `from 1 year the insurer may reject only with the Magistrates Court's leave (s 132(1))`
-- Rejected on day 18 only because there was no time to assess: no effect (s 130(2)).
#ASSERT `From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026` EQUALS `the rejection does not let weekly compensation stop: the insurer stays liable until it rejects or settles (s 134(1))` `the only ground is that the insurer has not had time to assess the claim (s 130(2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE I4. Recovering payments (s 128(2)(b), s 134(2)-(4)).
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `May I recover what I paid on the claim` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer may not recover it from the worker (s 128(2)(b), s 134(2))`
#ASSERT `May I recover what I paid on the claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer may not recover it from the worker, but may recover from the employer what the employer owes under s 95 (s 134(3))`
-- A self-insurer is the employer: s 134(3) does not apply to it (s 134(4)).
#ASSERT `May I recover what I paid on the claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the insurer may not recover it from the worker (s 128(2)(b), s 134(2))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Regulative rules (wca-core.l4).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 119. Clock in hours from receiving the claim. Deficient certificate flagged at hour 50; complying certificate at
-- hour 200: fulfilled (the claim is made at hour 200).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 119 -- a deficient medical certificate must be flagged within 72 hours, or the claim is taken to comply` FALSE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `tell the worker in writing what the medical certificate lacks` 50), (EVENT `the worker` `give a medical certificate that complies with s 118(2)` 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Flagged at hour 72 exactly: in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 119 -- a deficient medical certificate must be flagged within 72 hours, or the claim is taken to comply` FALSE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `tell the worker in writing what the medical certificate lacks` 72), (EVENT `the worker` `give a medical certificate that complies with s 118(2)` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not flagged by hour 72: the claim is taken to comply; nothing more is needed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 119 -- a deficient medical certificate must be flagged within 72 hours, or the claim is taken to comply` FALSE FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 73)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A complying certificate, or a waiver: nothing to flag.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 119 -- a deficient medical certificate must be flagged within 72 hours, or the claim is taken to comply` TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 119 -- a deficient medical certificate must be flagged within 72 hours, or the claim is taken to comply` FALSE TRUE) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the worker's giving of a complying certificate, pending (flagged at hour 50; until then no claim is made)
#TRACE `s 119 -- a deficient medical certificate must be flagged within 72 hours, or the claim is taken to comply` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `tell the worker in writing what the medical certificate lacks` AT 50

-- s 128. Clock in days from receiving the claim. Decided to reject on day 20, or day 28: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 128 -- the insurer is taken to accept a claim it has not decided to reject within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `decide to reject the claim` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 128 -- the insurer is taken to accept a claim it has not decided to reject within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `decide to reject the claim` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the insurer's prohibition on recovering payments made on the claim, in force (no decision by day 28)
#TRACE `s 128 -- the insurer is taken to accept a claim it has not decided to reject within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 128(2): the insurer did not decide to reject the claim within 28 days ..." (recovers on day 40)
#TRACE `s 128 -- the insurer is taken to accept a claim it has not decided to reject within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `recover a payment made on the claim` AT 40

-- ss 130-132, 134. Clock in days from the rejection. Rejected 20 November, may stop from 4 December: 14 days.
#ASSERT `days from` `20 Nov 2026` `to` `4 Dec 2026` EQUALS 14
-- Stopping on day 14: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 130-132, 134 -- after a rejection, the insurer must keep paying weekly compensation until the day it may stop` (`From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`) 14) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `stop paying weekly compensation` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "ss 130-132, 134(1): the insurer stopped weekly compensation before the day ..." (stopped on day 13)
#TRACE `ss 130-132, 134 -- after a rejection, the insurer must keep paying weekly compensation until the day it may stop` (`From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`) 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `stop paying weekly compensation` AT 13
-- Rejected 1 December, may stop from 26 January 2027: 56 days. Stopping on day 56: fulfilled.
#ASSERT `days from` `1 Dec 2026` `to` `26 Jan 2027` EQUALS 56
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 130-132, 134 -- after a rejection, the insurer must keep paying weekly compensation until the day it may stop` (`From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`) 56) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `stop paying weekly compensation` 56)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "ss 130-132, 134(1): ..." (stopped on day 55)
#TRACE `ss 130-132, 134 -- after a rejection, the insurer must keep paying weekly compensation until the day it may stop` (`From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `1 Dec 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`) 56 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `stop paying weekly compensation` AT 55
-- A rejection after 1 year without leave lets nothing stop. expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 134(1): the rejection does not take effect ..." (stopped on day 30)
#TRACE `ss 130-132, 134 -- after a rejection, the insurer must keep paying weekly compensation until the day it may stop` (`From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `3 Nov 2027` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`) 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `stop paying weekly compensation` AT 30
-- expect: the insurer's prohibition on stopping weekly compensation, still in force on day 400 (it has no end date)
#TRACE `ss 130-132, 134 -- after a rejection, the insurer must keep paying weekly compensation until the day it may stop` (`From what day may I stop paying weekly compensation after rejecting` `2 Nov 2026` `3 Nov 2027` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `2 Nov 2026`) 0 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
